Homepage: https://github.com/vomlehn/tcspecial
Description: tcspecial's configuration editor and checker
 The software tools that write and check tcspecial's configurations: tcs-cfge,
 the graphical configuration editor, with its node descriptions; tcs-verify,
 which says what is wrong with a configuration without running any of it;
 tcs-conflict, which says whether two configurations can be run at once;
 and tcs_ui, the Python window pieces the examples' ground stations show.
 Never flown; the manuals and examples are tcspecial-doc. Everything is
 under /opt/tcs, and a .pth file puts tcs_ui on python3's path.
 /etc/profile.d/tcs-tools.sh puts /opt/tcs/bin on a login shell's search
 path, and /opt/tcs/sbin/tcs-tools-links links the programs into
 /usr/local/bin for everything else.
